NO LICENSE HAS BEEN SELECTED.

The project owner must choose a licence. Until one is added, the default
is "all rights reserved": others may not legally copy, modify or reuse the code.

Common options:
- MIT: very permissive; keep copyright notice.
- Apache-2.0: permissive, with an explicit patent grant.
- GPL-3.0: copyleft; derivative works must also be GPL.
- AGPL-3.0: copyleft that also covers network/SaaS use.
- Proprietary / none: keep it private or source-available.

Pick one at https://choosealicense.com, replace this file with the full
licence text, and update the badge in README.md.
